# Copy to .env and fill in. No value here may be an absolute path, except
# WF_VAULT_ROOT (see the note below it).
WF_DB_PATH=./data/wf.db
# Optional: nothing reads either of these yet. Set them when a consumer exists.
# WF_DATA_DIR=./data
# WF_LOG_DIR=./logs
# Optional until M5. Leave unset if the vault is not mounted on this machine.
# Unlike the other paths above, this one MAY be absolute: an Obsidian vault
# lives outside the repo by definition, often in a cloud-synced directory the
# OS manages, so a relative path can't reach it portably. Either form works:
# WF_VAULT_ROOT=./vault/watchfloor
# WF_VAULT_ROOT=/srv/obsidian/watchfloor
WF_TZ=America/New_York
# Required. Checked on every route except /health (deliberately public — a
# liveness probe). Send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Pick a long
# random value; this is a real credential, not a placeholder to leave as-is.
WF_API_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
WF_API_PORT=8787
# OPTIONAL. A GitHub personal access token for the repos beat (M4a).
#
# Leave it unset — or blank, which is equivalent — and the client runs
# unauthenticated. That is a fully supported mode, not a degraded one; it just
# has a much smaller budget:
#
#                    Search API      Core API
#   unauthenticated   10 req/min     60 req/hour
#   with a PAT        30 req/min      5,000 req/hour
#
# So the token buys roughly 83x the core budget, which is the difference
# between polling a handful of topics once and enriching every repo it finds.
#
# Scope: READ-ONLY, and nothing more. A fine-grained token needs only "Public
# Repositories (read-only)"; a classic token needs NO scopes ticked at all —
# public repository data is readable with an unscoped token, and an unscoped
# token cannot write anything anywhere. Do not grant `repo`.
#
# Create it yourself at https://github.com/settings/tokens — no automation in
# this repository will, or may, do it for you.
#
# This is a real credential against your account, and this repository is
# PUBLIC. `.env` is gitignored; keep it that way, and never paste a token into
# a tracked file, an issue, or a commit message.
# WF_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Optional, default 60000 (60s). How often src/bin/scheduler.ts's tick loop
# checks which sources are due. Must be a positive integer no larger than
# 2147483647 (2^31 - 1) -- Node's setTimeout/setInterval delay ceiling;
# above it Node silently clamps to a 1ms tick rather than rejecting it.
# WF_SCHEDULER_TICK_INTERVAL_MS=60000
# OPTIONAL, and absent is the SHIPPED configuration. The Anthropic API
# credential for the M5 enrichment backend (src/enrich/llm/anthropic.ts).
#
# You almost certainly do not need this. config/llm.yaml selects `ollama`,
# which is local and free-forever; the Anthropic backend is built and
# hard-disabled per the M5 plan's RULING 2, for you to enable deliberately.
#
# ENABLING IT COSTS MONEY, and takes two variables, not one:
#
#   WF_ALLOW_PAID_ANTHROPIC=1     # the §15 cost gate — see docs/costs.md
#   WF_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# ...plus `backend: anthropic` in config/llm.yaml. With the flag unset the
# backend still loads and reports "disabled by cost policy" on every call, and
# sends nothing — tests/cost/no-paid-requests.test.ts proves that no request
# escapes, by blocking the socket layer and asserting zero attempts.
#
# A machine-wide ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately NOT used. If you have one
# exported for Claude Code, this project ignores it; a credential must be given
# to Watchfloor by name.
#
# Create the key yourself at https://console.anthropic.com — no automation in
# this repository will, or may, do it for you. This is a real billable
# credential and this repository is PUBLIC. `.env` is gitignored; keep it that
# way, and never paste a key into a tracked file, an issue, or a commit
# message.
# WF_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
